.TH "PAY_RESPECTS" "5" "April 2026" "pay\-respects 0.8.8" "Rule File"
.SH Writing Rules
Rule files live under rules.
Core parses them at build time.
The \f[CR]runtime\-rules\f[R] module reads them from the user
configuration at run time.
.PP
New rules should use version 2.
Version 1 still works, but the runtime module prints a warning when it
loads one.
.SS Locations
Runtime rules are loaded from:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R], default \f[CR]$HOME/.config\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\f[R], default \f[CR]/etc/xdg\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]XDG_DATA_DIRS\f[R], default \f[CR]/usr/local/share:/usr/share\f[R]
.PP
Place files under \f[CR]pay\-respects/rules/\f[R], for example
\f[CR]\(ti/.config/pay\-respects/rules/cargo.toml\f[R].
Name the file after the main command.
\f[CR]_PR_GENERAL.toml\f[R] is always parsed.
.SS Version 2
.IP
.EX
version = 2
commands = [\(dqhello\(dq, \(dqhi\(dq]

\f[B][[match]]\f[R]
\f[I]# Error patterns are optional. A match without patterns always runs.\f[R]
error = [
    \(dqpattern 1\(dq,
    \(dqpattern 2\(dq,
]
vars = { dir = \(dq{{command[1]}}\(dq }

\f[B][[match.suggest]]\f[R]
\f[I]# Conditions are checked before the suggestion is used.\f[R]
when = [
    \(dqexecutable(sudo)\(dq,
    \(dq!cmd_contains(sudo)\(dq,
]
run = \(dqsudo {{command}}\(dq

\f[B][[match.suggest]]\f[R]
when = [\(dqlength(2)\(dq]
inline = true
run = \(dq{{command[0]}} fix {{command[1]}}\(dq

\f[B][[match.suggest]]\f[R]
run = \(dqcd {{$dir}}\(dq

\f[B][[match.suggest]]\f[R]
function = \(dqMyRustFunction\(dq

\f[B][[match.suggest]]\f[R]
script = { interpreter = \(dq/usr/bin/python3\(dq, file = \(dqgit\-fix.py\(dq }
.EE
.PP
Fields:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]version\f[R]: \f[CR]2\f[R] for this format.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]commands\f[R]: Command names that share the file.
Aliases go here.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]error\f[R]: Case and whitespace insensitive substrings from the
error output.
Omit it to always match.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]vars\f[R]: Optional variables for the match.
Use a table or an array of \f[CR][name, value]\f[R] pairs.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]when\f[R]: Conditions, one string per condition.
Conditions are ANDed.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]inline\f[R]: Also allow the suggestion in inline mode.
Patterns are ignored in inline mode.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]run\f[R]: One suggestion template.
Use another \f[CR][[match.suggest]]\f[R] block for another suggestion.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]function\f[R]: Call a Rust function from
\f[CR]rules_function.rs\f[R].
Runtime rules skip it because they cannot run Rust functions.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]script\f[R]: Run a script with an external interpreter.
Use exactly one of \f[CR]run\f[R], \f[CR]function\f[R], or
\f[CR]script\f[R].
.PP
Variables are expanded before the suggestion template is parsed.
A value can use placeholders or other variables, so \f[CR]{{$dir}}\f[R]
also works inside another placeholder.
Unknown variables and cycles fail at parse time.
.PP
The pair form is useful when variable order matters:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][[match]]\f[R]
vars = [
    [\(dqcmd\(dq, \(dq{{command[0]}}\(dq],
    [\(dqarg\(dq, \(dq{{command[1]}}\(dq],
]
.EE
.PP
Each condition is its own string.
A comma inside a regex does not need escaping.
.SS Scripts
\f[CR]script\f[R] runs a script with an external interpreter.
Scripts are only available in runtime rules.
Core rejects them at build time.
.IP
.EX
\f[B][[match.suggest]]\f[R]
script = { interpreter = \(dq/usr/bin/python3\(dq, file = \(dqgit\-fix.py\(dq }
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]file\f[R] can be absolute.
A relative path is searched in these directories:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pay\-respects/scripts\f[R], default
\f[CR]$HOME/.config/pay\-respects/scripts\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/pay\-respects/scripts\f[R], default
\f[CR]/etc/xdg/pay\-respects/scripts\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]XDG_DATA_DIRS/pay\-respects/scripts\f[R], default
\f[CR]/usr/local/share/pay\-respects/scripts:/usr/share/pay\-respects/scripts\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
The directory of the rule file
.PP
The interpreter is run with the script file as its only argument.
This works with Python, Lua, Node, shell, and other interpreters that
accept a file path.
.PP
The script gets the same environment variables as a module:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]_PR_COMMAND\f[R]: Command without arguments
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]_PR_LAST_COMMAND\f[R]: Full command
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]_PR_ERROR_MSG\f[R]: Error message
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]_PR_SHELL\f[R]: Current shell
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]_PR_EXECUTABLES\f[R]: Executables separated by spaces.
Empty when the list is too large.
.PP
Print suggestions to \f[CR]stdout\f[R].
Separate multiple suggestions with \f[CR]<_PR_BR>\f[R].
Without the separator, each non\-empty line becomes one suggestion.
.PP
Variables are substituted in \f[CR]interpreter\f[R] and \f[CR]file\f[R]
before they are used.
.SS Version 1 (deprecated)
.IP
.EX
command = \(dqhello\(dq
extends = [\(dqgoodbye\(dq]

\f[B][[match_err]]\f[R]
pattern = [
    \(dqpattern 1\(dq,
]
suggest = [
\(aq\(aq\(aq
#[executable(sudo), !cmd_contains(sudo)]
sudo {{command}} \(aq\(aq\(aq
]
.EE
.PP
In version 1, \f[CR]extends\f[R] lists aliases.
Conditions go inside a \f[CR]#[...]\f[R] block at the start of the
suggestion.
Commas inside a regex must be escaped as \f[CR]\(rs,\f[R].
.PP
Version 1 remains supported at run time.
Migrate to version 2 before it is removed.
.SS Placeholders
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{command}}\f[R]: The full command without changes
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{command[1]}}\f[R]: The first argument.
The command itself is index 0.
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
Negative values count from the end.
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{command[2:5]}}\f[R]: Arguments from index 2 through index 5.
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
An empty side starts at the beginning or ends at the last argument.
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{typo[2](fix1, fix2)}}\f[R]: Replace the second argument with the
closest candidate.
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
A candidate list needs at least two values.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]path\f[R] searches executables in \f[CR]$PATH\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]file\f[R] searches files on disk.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{shell(<command>)}}\f[R] uses each output line as a candidate.
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{select[3](one, two)}}\f[R]: Create one suggestion per selection.
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
Only one \f[CR]select\f[R] is allowed in a template.
.IP \(bu 2
Use \f[CR]{{selection}}\f[R] to place the same selection in another
position.
.IP \(bu 2
The index is optional and only affects \f[CR]path\f[R].
It defaults to \f[CR]0\f[R].
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{opt::<Regular Expression>}}\f[R]: Remove the captured patterns
from the command before later placeholders run.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{cmd::<Regular Expression>}}\f[R]: Insert the captures from the
command.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{err::<Regular Expression>}}\f[R]: Insert the captures from the
error message.
Matching is case\-sensitive.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]{{shell(<command>)}}\f[R]: Insert the output of a shell command.
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
Inside \f[CR]typo\f[R] or \f[CR]select\f[R], each output line becomes a
candidate or selection.
.RE
.PP
Regex syntax follows \c
.UR https://docs.rs/regex-lite/latest/regex_lite/#syntax
regex\-lite
.UE \c
\&.
.SS Conditions
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]executable\f[R]: The argument is in \f[CR]$PATH\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]cmd_contains\f[R]: The last command matches the regex
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]err_contains\f[R]: The error message matches the regex, ignoring
case and whitespace
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]length\f[R]: The command has exactly this many arguments
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]min_length\f[R]: The command has at least this many arguments
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]max_length\f[R]: The command has at most this many arguments
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]shell\f[R]: The current shell equals the argument
.PP
Prefix a condition with \f[CR]!\f[R] to negate it.
.SS Other Considerations
When a suggestion chains commands with \f[CR]&&\f[R], prefer multiple
lines.
.IP \(bu 2
Long commands read better that way.
.IP \(bu 2
The shell integration can convert \f[CR]&&\f[R] where the shell does not
support it, for example Nushell.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][[match.suggest]]\f[R]
run = \(aq\(aq\(aq
command1 &&
command2 \(aq\(aq\(aq
.EE
